# Glowcap Lantern: it grants its abilities only to the creature it is attached to (CR 301.5, 613.1f; its ruling: "If Glowcap
# Lantern isn't attached to a creature you control, you can't look at the top card of your library"). Turn 1 the Lantern is
# equipped to the Ornithopter. Turn 2 Bot2's Shock kills the Ornithopter: the Lantern stays on the battlefield unattached,
# Bot1 may no longer look, and on turn 3 the Memnite that attacks explores nothing - the Lightning Bolt stays unrevealed.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Ornithopter
Memnite
Glowcap Lantern
Island
Island
Lightning Bolt
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Shock
Mountain x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Glowcap Lantern.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Glowcap Lantern.Activate(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.MayLookAtLibraryTop = true
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Shock.Cast(Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter
? Bot1.MayLookAtLibraryTop = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Glowcap Lantern; Memnite; Mox Emerald; Mox Jet; Mox Pearl
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Hand = Island; Island
Bot1.Library.Count = 12
